    "explanation": "To both parties: the $4.00 cancellation fee does not stand. The rider is refunded in full and the driver receives no compensation.\n\nDriver — the trip was closed by you with the reason code DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE, and POL-NS-01 accepts only RIDER_NO_SHOW, RIDER_UNREACHABLE or EXCESSIVE_WAIT. A driver who reports that he could not find the rider has not recorded a rider no-show, so the fee is not chargeable on that code, and the trip is decided under POL-NS-03. Independently of that, the GPS trace never places your vehicle inside the 50 m arrival radius at Blk 118 at any point in the trip — your closest approach across all 92 fixes was 259.94 m — so there is no admissible arrival, and there is 0 seconds of in-geofence dwell against the 300 seconds a STANDARD pickup requires. POL-NS-06 makes the refund compulsory on that shortfall alone, whether or not the rider was present and whether or not messages were exchanged.\n\nRider — the same outcome follows on the wrong-entrance route, POL-NS-03. The driver's closest approach (259.94 m) is outside the 50 m arrival radius but inside the clause's 400 m ceiling, and the trip record shows he marked arrival at 07:26:40 and did not cancel until 07:33:05. On that route the fee is still refunded in full; the only additional question is who absorbs the cost, and that is decided from the chat. You stated 'blk 118, the one facing the carpark' at 07:22:10, which matches the registered pickup 'Blk 118 Rivervale Dr, Sengkang'; the driver answered 'ok coming' at 07:22:48 and read it at 07:23:02, yet never moved to that block before cancelling. Under POL-NS-03(i) the driver therefore bears the loss and is owed nothing. Pin-ambiguity goodwill under POL-NS-03(ii) is unavailable: the trip registers a single pickup point, not two or more, and the driver's account of where the app pin sat is supported by no venue_id and by no party statement in the chat.\n\nEvidence quality: the chat log EV-CHAT-00205 is impaired at weight 0.8 because its issue code CONTENT_REDACTED removed the unit number from the rider's first message. The block identifier on which the fault allocation turns survives intact, so that finding survives the discount. The GPS trace and trip record, which carry the facts that decide the refund, are both at full weight 1.0, so confidence is not capped below the floor.\n\nNo escalation is required and no referral is entered: the two parties have no other no-show dispute between them in the trailing 90 days, the rider has one no-show dispute in 30 days, and the driver's anti-farming check does not trip (2 no-show terminations against 104 completed trips, both limbs of POL-NS-07 clear). The $4.00 charged to the rider is returned to the rider."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The driver's pin-ambiguity answer is unavailable on the record twice over. POL-NS-03(ii) requires trip_record.registered_pickup_points of 2 or more, and this trip registers exactly 1. And POL-NS-03 forbids any assertion that a coordinate is a particular venue, block or entrance except on a venue_id or on a party statement in the chat log; the driver's claim that 'the pin in my app showed the carpark side' rests on no venue_id comparison and no chat statement, so it establishes nothing.",
